    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0742" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1012/–4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                            1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information a copy of a dispatch from the legation in Guatemala City,
                    transmitting correspondence relating to the exercise of the good offices of the
                    American chargé d’affaires ad interim in behalf of Mr. Ramon Chan, who is
                    referred to as presumably of Chinese nationality.</p>
                <p>It would appear that the Chinese nationality of Mr. Ramon Chan had not been
                    positively ascertained, but had been inferred from his name.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
